    "explanation": "To the rider: your claim is upheld. To the driver: no route deviation is found against you on this trip; the money refunded to the rider comes from the platform fare, not from your earnings.\n\nROUTE. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-00702) is complete — 100% coverage, 115 fixes at a 10 s cadence, no gaps — and measures 10.99 km against a platform optimal of 11.00 km, an excess of −0.01 km (−0.09%). Neither POL-RD-01 gate (excess above 20% of optimal, and above 0.80 km) is met, so no route deviation exists, and the dropoff-pin amendment at 09:27:40 does not change that: re-run on the amended endpoints under POL-RD-05, the stored amended optimal is 11.00 km / 19 min (identical to the booked optimal) and the trace again sits below it. The driver's traffic explanation under POL-RD-03 has no advisory to stand on — EV-ADVIS-00702-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT, disclosed by the rider — and nothing turns on it, because there is no measured deviation to exonerate.\n\nFARE. The trip is UPFRONT_QUOTE (fare_model UPFRONT_QUOTE, quoted_fare_sgd non-null), so POL-RD-02 does not run and no distance-or-time refund is available; POL-RD-11 governs. Under POL-RD-11(a) the rider recovers the amount by which charged_total exceeds the fare fixed at booking. The fare fixed at booking was SGD 13.80, recorded contemporaneously in the trip's own chat log (EV-CHAT-00702, weight 1.0): at 09:26:50 the driver wrote 'Just move the pin to Block B, same price', and at 09:27:45 the rider reported the app now said 22.40, not 13.80. The pin move was costless — the amended optimal equals the booked optimal — so the re-quote to SGD 22.40 has no distance or time behind it. Charged_total SGD 22.40 less the booking fare SGD 13.80 = SGD 8.60, rounded up to the nearest SGD 0.05 = SGD 8.60, which is the whole of the contested amount (SGD 8.60) and is returned in full. No pass-through correction is added or netted: no ERP gantries, no tolls, no airport surcharge and no waiting-time fee (properly_chargeable total SGD 0.00).\n\nThe driver's contrary points. The assertion that 'no SGD 13.80 quote appears on any admitted artifact' is not correct: the chat log is an admitted artifact at weight 1.0 and it carries the figure. The platform's own ledger shows quoted_fare_sgd = charged_total = SGD 22.40 (charged_over_quote SGD 0.00), but that quoted figure is the disputed post-amendment re-quote; POL-RD-11 fixes the fare at booking, and the booking fare is what the refund is measured against. The driver otherwise succeeds on the points that do not move money: no repeat-deviation pattern (driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d 0 over completed_trips_90d 250), so no POL-RD-06 uplift and no conduct referral; and no driver compensation under POL-RD-04, because the billed 11.0 km is not less than the trace's 10.99 km and there is no unbilled distance.\n\nThe rider's request to escalate under POL-RD-10(7) is declined: the ledger's SGD 22.40 records the re-quote rather than a competing booking quote, and the driver's own 'same price' message corroborates the rider, so the two records are not mutually contradictory evidence of comparable strength. As an open observation (not a referral), the platform may wish to review why a distance-neutral pin move triggered an SGD 8.60 re-quote.\n\nConfidence 0.85, capped by the weight-1.0 artifacts that carry the deciding facts (EV-CHAT-00702 for the booking fare and the driver's assurance, EV-FARE-00702 for the charged total)."
