{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 8.60,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.8,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: the rider is entitled to the whole of the SGD 8.60 she contests.\n\nWhat is not in dispute: the destination pin was moved mid-trip (dropoff_amended_at 2026-09-22T09:27:40) and the platform issued a new fare. The route itself is clean. The driver's GPS trace (EV-GPS-00702) has 100% coverage, 115 fixes at a 10 s cadence and no gaps, and measures 10.99 km against an optimal of 11.0 km; the amended optimal stored on the trip record (EV-TRIP-00702) is also 11.0 km / 19 min, identical to the booked optimal. Moving the pin about 80 m added no distance and no time, so there is no deviation under POL-RD-01, none survives the POL-RD-05 re-run, and no distance or time refund is available on an UPFRONT_QUOTE trip because POL-RD-02 does not run (POL-RD-11).\n\nThe disputed question is what the fare was fixed at before the move. The fare ledger (EV-FARE-00702) records quoted_fare_sgd 22.40 and charged_total 22.40, so its own POL-RD-11(a) figure is 0.00. But the ledger was written at 09:38:00, after the 09:27:40 amendment, and the driver's own statement concedes that 'the platform issued the new quote'. The 22.40 on the ledger is therefore the post-amendment re-quote, not the figure fixed at booking that POL-RD-11(a) protects. The booking figure is recorded contemporaneously in the trip's chat log (EV-CHAT-00702, admitted at weight 1.0 with no issue codes): at 09:26:50 the driver wrote 'Just move the pin to Block B, same price', and at 09:27:45 the rider replied 'I changed it and the app now says 22.40, not 13.80'. The rider was on SGD 13.80.\n\nApplying POL-RD-11(a): charged_total SGD 22.40 less the fare fixed at booking SGD 13.80 = SGD 8.60, refunded in full (well above the SGD 0.50 de minimis, and the whole contested amount). Nothing offsets it: the ledger carries no ERP or toll lines, no airport surcharge (the trip did not originate at an airport) and no waiting-time fee, and the properly chargeable total is SGD 0.00, so POL-RD-09 gives no standalone correction and no deduction.\n\nOn the arguments raised. I accept that the trace shows no deviation and that the rider edited the pin herself, but the driver's assurance of 'same price' in the same chat is why this fare consequence falls on the platform rather than the rider. I do not accept the driver's assertion that no SGD 13.80 figure appears on any admitted artifact: it appears in the rider's message on the chat log. I accept that no repeat-deviation pattern exists (driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 over 250 completed trips), so no POL-RD-06 uplift or conduct referral follows, and that no driver compensation arises (billed 11.0 km is not below the traced 10.99 km, POL-RD-04). The rider's alternative request that the case be escalated as undecidable under POL-RD-10 is declined: the driver's concession that a new quote was issued resolves which quote the ledger holds, so the record decides the case. The missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-00702-01, weight 0.0) is noted, but no traffic cause was asserted, so POL-RD-03 and POL-RD-13 have nothing to work on; no charge line is unmatched, so POL-RD-09(4) produces no billing-integrity referral.\n\nThe finding rests on the chat log, the artifact that carries the deciding booking-fare fact, admitted at weight 1.0; confidence is set at 0.80, above the 0.70 floor."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

