    "explanation": "To both parties: I cannot decide this one on the record, so it goes to a human reviewer and the contested SGD 8.60 is held — neither collected nor refunded. Here is why. ROUTE. The route itself is not in dispute. The driver's GPS trace measures 10.99 km against a platform optimal of 11.0 km (EV-GPS-00702, EV-TRIP-00702), so there is no excess distance at all, let alone one meeting POL-RD-01's gates of more than 20% of optimal and more than 0.8 km. The destination pin was moved at 09:27:40 and the stored amended optimal is still 11.0 km over 19 min, so re-running the test on the amended endpoints under POL-RD-05 leaves no deviation either. On distance, the driver is right and no distance refund is available. FARE. This was an upfront-quoted trip (EV-FARE-00702), so POL-RD-11 governs and the only money question is whether the amount charged exceeds the fare fixed at booking. Two records of comparable weight disagree on what that fare was. The fare ledger records quoted_fare_sgd of SGD 22.40 against a charge of SGD 22.40 — equal, so POL-RD-11(a)'s arithmetic gives SGD 0.00 and no refund can be read off the fare breakdown. But the rider's in-app message, sent at 09:27:45 from inside the trip, records the app showing SGD 13.80 immediately before the pin was moved and SGD 22.40 immediately after (EV-CHAT-00702), and the driver's own statement concedes that 'the platform issued the new quote.' At face value the rider is SGD 8.60 out of pocket; on the recorded quote she is not. The driver's assertion that no SGD 13.80 figure appears on any admitted artifact is not correct — it appears in the chat log, which is admitted at weight 1.0. ESCALATION. Both sides are therefore supported by admissible, mutually contradictory evidence of comparable strength (both weight 1.0) on the single fact that decides the money — which quoted fare was fixed at booking. That is the POL-RD-10(7) trigger, and it is terminal: no monetary outcome issues. What would resolve it is the platform's own booking-time quote record for this trip (the pre-amendment quote), which is not in the bundle. OTHER POINTS, none of which change the outcome. No repeat-deviation pattern is established (0 flags in 90 days over 250 trips, POL-RD-06), so no driver-conduct referral is made and none of POL-RD-06(a)-(c) fires. No ERP, toll, airport-surcharge or waiting-time line exists to correct (POL-RD-09), and no billing-integrity defect under POL-RD-09(4). The missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00702-01 (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) changes nothing, because no party relied on an external traffic cause (POL-RD-13). No unbilled-distance compensation is due (POL-RD-04)."
